  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indigenous Artisan Capacity-Building, Law Promotion and Museum Construction</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIDAC will increase the workmanship and incomes of 200 artisans from Guaranies, Weenhawek, Ayoreo, and other indigenous and mestizo peoples in eastern Bolivia. The project will foster skills and product development for pottery, woodcarving, weaving and other crafts, construct the first stages of an indigenous arts museum, and provide a current report on the artisan sector for eastern and southern Bolivia though activities in training, technical assistance, and museum development. The project will foment broader appreciation for these cultural values, increase the incomes of the beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
